#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# convex_optimization

#% text
# `convex_optimization(f, cons, vars)` gives the point at which the convex function `f` is smallest under the constraints `cons`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `cons` is a list of equations and inequalities, read as their conjunction; `vars` is a variable or a list of variables.

#% item
# The problem is passed to `minimize`, which treats it by its general methods.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
convex_optimization(x^2 + y^2, [x + y >= 2], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 1, y -> 1]

#% cell
convex_optimization((x - 1)^2 + (y - 2)^2, [x + y <= 2], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 1/2, y -> 3/2]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `linear_optimization`, `minimize`
